From 7f2ce28188cdd11096c9bb2fddcedb619933b10a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:52:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: drive-mode decode (CLU13 CF_Clu_DriveMode) ->
 CarStateSP.driveMode + personality mapping

The cluster broadcasts the current drive mode on CLU13 (0x50C) byte5 HIGH nibble; add it as a
first-class DBC signal and expose it to the control layer.

- DBC (opendbc/dbc/generator/hyundai/hyundai_can.dbc): new signal CF_Clu_DriveMode 44|4 (bits 44-47
  were undefined; no collision with CF_Clu_EcoDriveInf 40|3 or CF_Clu_IsaMainSW 43|1) with the mode
  values documented; CM_ notes that on CN7 the EcoDriveInf low nibble carries the N-custom slot and
  that MDPS11 CF_Mdps_CurrMode is a steering-mode level (0 normal / 1 sport / 3 N), not an alive
  counter; VAL_ for CF_Mdps_CurrMode. Decode from route 00000147 (car-features/0x4a0-decode.md).
- drive_mode.py: pure mapping DriveModeResult (1 normal -> standard, 2 eco -> relaxed, 3 sport ->
  aggressive, 6/7 N-custom/N -> BLOCK, else UNKNOWN) and a one-source-frame debouncer.
- carstate_ext.py: read CLU13 CF_Clu_DriveMode off the C-CAN parser (vl_all, debounced one frame) into
  the new CarStateSP.driveMode (capnp + structs.py mirror, coupled pair like speedLimit).

Additive only; no opendbc/safety and no panda changes (no firmware impact).
